From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AppSandbox contributors <appsandbox@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clutter: flush the AppSandbox D3D12 output after paint

The hook is placed after the default `paint-view` handler, while the stage
view framebuffer is still the compositor's output and before the native
backend submits/presents it. Mesa's AppSandbox d3d12 hook consumes the current
Gallium framebuffer at the following flush and performs the GPU-only copy into
its shared ring.

The environment guard is deterministic: only an AppSandbox compositor with
ASB_D3D12_DISPLAY=1 enables the extra flush. Normal Mutter sessions do not
acquire the extra flush or open the AppSandbox socket. The patch does not
change appsandbox-display, KMS, GBM modifiers, PRIME, DMA-BUF, or scanout.

Hook point: `clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c`, `_clutter_stage_paint_view`,
immediately after the `paint-view` signal/default handler returns.

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
@@ -463,5 +463,9 @@ clutter_stage_paint_view (ClutterStage     *stage,
     g_signal_emit (stage, stage_signals[PAINT_VIEW], 0, view, redraw_clip, frame);
   else
     CLUTTER_STAGE_GET_CLASS (stage)->paint_view (stage, view, redraw_clip, frame);
+
+  /* Publish the actual compositor output through Mesa's opt-in GPU ring. */
+  if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("ASB_D3D12_DISPLAY"), "1") == 0)
+    cogl_framebuffer_flush (clutter_stage_view_get_framebuffer (view));
 }
 void
